# Machine-generated junk from R, RStudio, macOS, and Claude Code. None of it is
# project content: .RData/.Rhistory are whatever happened to be in a local session,
# and committing them makes every collaborator's diff noisy for no benefit.
.Rhistory
.RData
.RDataTmp
.Rproj.user/
.DS_Store
.claude/

# EVERYTHING under data/ stays local and is never pushed. This is a deliberate
# protection rule, not housekeeping -- do not narrow it without a good reason:
#   * PEOPLE   -- data/project_info/rosters/*.csv hold volunteer and identifier
#                 personal contact details (email, phone). Publishing those would
#                 expose private information about people who volunteered.
#   * CREDENTIALS -- data/secrets/ holds live API keys (inat_api.env, iucn_api.env).
#                 A key pushed to a public repo is compromised the moment it lands.
#   * PARK DATA -- specimen and observation tables carry precise coordinates for
#                 bees inside a National Monument, including at-risk species.
#                 Exact localities for sensitive taxa are not ours to publish.
# The public site in docs/ is built FROM this data but contains only the aggregated,
# non-sensitive outputs. If you need the raw data, see DATA_ACCESS.md -- it is shared
# person to person, not through this repo.
/data

# THE PUBLISHED WEBSITE. This is the one place the rules are inverted: docs/* is
# ignored by default and specific file types are allow-listed back in with "!".
# Why: GitHub Pages serves this folder to the public, so only finished web assets
# belong here (HTML pages, images, and .nojekyll which stops GitHub from trying to
# process the site with Jekyll). The allow-list means a stray CSV, script, or note
# dropped into docs/ is ignored rather than silently published. If you add a genuinely
# new web asset type (a .css or .svg, say), you must add a matching "!" line or it
# will never be pushed and the live site will look broken.
docs/*
!docs/*.html
!docs/.nojekyll
!docs/*.jpg
!docs/*.jpeg
!docs/*.webp
!docs/*.png

# Test suite kept LOCAL (2026-08-24). Nothing here is called by the cleaning,
# analysis, or publishing pipelines -- see tests/README.md. Tracked copies were
# removed from the repo; the files still live on this machine.
/tests

# NOTE: dev-docs/ is deliberately TRACKED (since 2026-08-24). It holds the pipeline
# guide, the manual-inputs list, pitfalls, and the specimen changelog -- the working
# knowledge a new maintainer needs, and CLAUDE.md points at it by name. It was
# ignored until now; it was reviewed before publishing and contains no personal
# contact details, credentials, or species coordinates. Keep it that way.

# PDFs anywhere in the repo: conference decks, downloaded papers, exported reports.
# GitHub rejects any file over 100 MB, and a talk deck full of photos blows past that
# and would block the push entirely. Reference papers live in data/reference/source/.
*.pdf

# Scratch-file naming convention. Anything a person names _v_something, _check_...,
# _fresh_..., etc. is a work-in-progress copy, so the pattern keeps half-finished
# experiments out of the repo automatically. Use these prefixes on purpose when you
# want a file to stay local.
_v_*
_fresh_*
_final_*
_check_*
_verify_*
_scratch*
